what do you do when you fall off track  I'm going to answer that question in  today's episode of ask Evan sorry mr.  got a question for one of my loyal  youtube viewers and TGIM mastermind  members psyched to go who asked could  you talk about how to overcome feelings  of edginess  or dread like for example days when you  don't have enough sleep or you wake up  past your intended time and don't get to  do your morning routine anymore but when  you are worrying about something outside  your work I really like the mindset  stuff this is a fantastic question and I  think this really depends on your  personality I know for me when I miss my  morning routine I have a high likelihood  of my whole day blowing up on me and so  I'm gonna share with you the three  things that I do that hopefully can help  you with your process number one is try  to do something valuable this is  probably the hardest thing for me but if  I've missed my morning routine or I get  interrupted a lot you know I get that's  why I don't have phone calls anymore  because I don't want people interrupting  me in my day I still try to get back on  track and try to get back into a  schedule where I can provide some value  for that day this makes it really easy  when I've committed to somebody else so  for example on Wednesday I do all my  videos I've got Jason here coming to see  me and so I have to do videos on  Wednesday you know if I miss my water  routine Jason's still coming at noon I  still got the videos up I know you guys  are expecting them and so does that  external pressure to keep going on  Thursdays I have my meetings of  interviews coffee appointments phone  calls and all of those again I'm not  gonna miss because I've committed to  somebody else so when I've committed to  somebody else I'm much more likely to  get back on track where if I haven't  committed to somebody else and I don't  have anything to like pressuring me  right away I find a lot harder honestly  to get back on schedule and so my my  trick I guess is in that case try not to  fall off schedule in the first place  because I know how important my schedule  is for me personally I try to keep to it  as much as possible and try to design a  life where I don't have interruptions I  try to run what I call a no crisis  business  I hate being reactionary I hate playing  defense and just reacting to people's  problems instead I like being proactive  and attacking the new challenges are  that are ahead of me and you know  planning my schedule out as I want it to  be instead of being instead of reacting  to what other people want me to do  number two is explore something new what  I find is that if my day has blown up on  me and I just can't get back on track  and I haven't committed anybody else for  the day instead of just playing League  of Legends all day I'll try to just try  something new I'll try to break out take  on a project I haven't tried before look  at my list of ideas and try to tackle  those just try to get in that space - to  get me out of thinking that the whole  day is gone I find this is me personally  that if I try to get back on track with  a day that I've known is already kind of  falling sideways then I'm not committed  to those projects as much where instead  I try something new and totally  different I get energized again I have  passion again I can attack it with with  new eyes and I'm ready to go and do it  so if my day goes and blows up on me  then I try to go and find something new  to work on that still adds value but  maybe wasn't what I already scheduled  for the day and number three is start on  time tomorrow and that may seem really  basic but if you threw away your day you  woke up late you missed some  appointments you didn't get the work  done that you needed you goofed off and  went rips ticking all day or whatever it  was and you feel like crap at the end of  the day thinking man I didn't get  anything done today because you missed  your morning start then start on time  tomorrow right get a good night's sleep  set that alarm you wake up and whatever  the first thing is that you do for me  it's a gratitude exercise that I go  through whatever that first thing is  that you do start with that right away  as soon as you wake up and get your day  off to a good start the next day around  so those are my tips and again it's  highly personalized to me because the  schedule is so important for me to be a  happy and successful person I know a lot  of people are way more flexible than I  am and so again I encourage you to  design a life and a lifestyle that fits  who you are and allows you to leverage  your strengths so I'd love to know from  what do you do when you fall off track  when your date explodes on you you wake  up late whatever reason your day isn't  going as you would planned how do you  handle it I'd love to hear from you in  the comments below thank you so much for  watching  continue to believe and I'll see you  soon
 

